John worked twice as long as Jill on Saturday.
Saturday hours John worked = 2 * 2 = 4 hours.
John worked three times as long as Jill on Sunday.
Sunday hours John worked = 3 * 1 = 3 hours.
Total hours John worked = 4 + 3 = 7 hours.
John's earnings = 7 * $10 = $70.
The difference between John's earnings and Jill's earnings is $70 - $30 = $40.
John earned $40 more than Jill.

